    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Project case study / 02</div>
    <h1><span class="gradient">SystemPulse</span></h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Local-First System Intelligence &amp; Behavioral Analysis — an independent
      project exploring how hardware telemetry, process activity, network
      observations, and historical context can help explain system behavior.
    </p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary"
         href="https://github.com/nachiketnarkhede/SystemPulse"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore source repository ↗</a>

      <a class="button"
         href="https://github.com/nachiketnarkhede/SystemPulse-Independent-Research-Paper-Local-First-System-Intelligence-Behavioral-Analysis"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Research paper repository ↗</a>

      <a class="button"
         href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nachiket-narkhede"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">01 / Overview</div>
        <h2>From raw telemetry to system context.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">THE PROBLEM</div>
          <h3>Metrics do not always explain behavior</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            CPU utilization, memory consumption, disk activity, processes,
            and network connections are useful observations. Viewed separately,
            however, they may not explain why a system is behaving unusually.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">THE PROJECT IDEA</div>
          <h3>Connect observations with context</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            SystemPulse is designed to bring system observations into a
            unified architecture and explore how history, behavioral deviations,
            evidence, and explanations can support deeper system understanding.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">02 / Conceptual architecture</div>
        <h2>A system-level view.</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          This diagram summarizes the processing concept described in the
          project README. It is not a performance benchmark or proof that
          every stage is fully implemented.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Conceptual SystemPulse analysis pipeline">
          <div class="stage">
            <strong>01. Observe</strong>
            <span>System telemetry</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stage">
            <strong>02. Organize</strong>
            <span>Structured state</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stage">
            <strong>03. Compare</strong>
            <span>History and deviations</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stage">
            <strong>04. Explain</strong>
            <span>Evidence and context</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">Local-first design</span>
          <span class="tag">Behavioral context</span>
          <span class="tag">System observability</span>
          <span class="tag">Explainable findings</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">03 / Areas of analysis</div>
        <h2>What the platform explores.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">01 — TELEMETRY</div>
          <h3>Hardware and resource activity</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            CPU, memory, disk, device, and related system observations provide
            a view of the machine's current state.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">02 — PROCESS CONTEXT</div>
          <h3>Connecting activity to software</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Process information can help put resource changes into context
            and identify areas that may need further investigation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">03 — NETWORK OBSERVATIONS</div>
          <h3>Connectivity and endpoints</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Network and Wi-Fi observations add another dimension to understanding
            system state and changes in connectivity.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">04 — BEHAVIORAL ANALYSIS</div>
          <h3>History and deviations</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Comparing observations with recent behavior can provide context
            for changes that might otherwise appear as isolated numbers.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">05 — RISK-AWARE INTERPRETATION</div>
          <h3>Separate observation from conclusion</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            An unusual reading is not automatically a security threat.
            Context and evidence matter before a finding can be interpreted.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="number">06 — REPORTING</div>
          <h3>Evidence that can be reviewed</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            The project describes reporting and research-oriented features
            intended to help users preserve observations and examine system behavior.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">04 / Design principles</div>
        <h2>Engineering beyond the dashboard.</h2>
      </div>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="principle">
          <strong>Observe before judging</strong>
          <p>A CPU spike or listening endpoint is an observation, not automatically a diagnosis or vulnerability.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <strong>Prefer local-first processing</strong>
          <p>System telemetry can be sensitive. The project describes a design that prioritizes local collection and analysis.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <strong>Keep explanations connected to evidence</strong>
          <p>Useful system intelligence should communicate why a finding matters instead of presenting an unexplained score alone.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <strong>Consider behavior over time</strong>
          <p>A resource level can mean different things depending on recent activity and what the machine is doing.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">05 / Technical direction</div>
        <h2>Where systems and intelligence meet.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>System observability</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Exploring how individual telemetry sources can contribute to a
            broader understanding of machine behavior.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Explainable system intelligence</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Exploring how evidence and context can help make system findings
            easier to interpret and investigate.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Privacy-aware architecture</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Considering the importance of keeping potentially sensitive
            machine observations local wherever the architecture permits.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Research and evaluation</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Further evaluation can examine detection quality, false positives,
            resource overhead, cross-platform behavior, and the limits of
            behavioral interpretation.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">06 / Limitations</div>
        <h2>Evidence matters.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        SystemPulse should not be treated as a guaranteed malware detector or
        a substitute for established security tools. An anomaly is not proof
        of malicious activity. Actual capabilities, platform compatibility,
        and implementation status should be checked against the source code
        and project documentation. This page does not claim independent
        validation or benchmark results.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-label">07 / Project resources</div>
        <h2>Explore the original work.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>SystemPulse source repository</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Read the project overview, inspect its structure, and review the
          implementation and current development status.
        </p>
        <p><a class="inline-link"
          href="https://github.com/nachiketnarkhede/SystemPulse"
          target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open source repository ↗</a></p>

        <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Independent research-paper repository</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          A separate repository associated with the local-first system
          intelligence and behavioral analysis topic.
        </p>
        <p><a class="inline-link"
          href="https://github.com/nachiketnarkhede/SystemPulse-Independent-Research-Paper-Local-First-System-Intelligence-Behavioral-Analysis"
          target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open research-paper repository ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Project note:</strong> This case study summarizes the project's
        stated direction and concepts. The source repository remains the
        reference for implementation details, current functionality, and
        project status. Inclusion of a research-paper repository does not
        imply peer-reviewed publication.
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

